{"id":1843,"level":74,"name":"Форсовані шахи","group":"Форсовані ходи","format":27,"description":"<p>In the previous lessons,&nbsp;Opposing pieces of the defending side were already on the same line (file, rank or diagonal). In the next three lessons, you will learn that by playing forcing moves, you can also get pieces that are not yet on the same line to be on the same line one move later. Then a skewer&nbsp;wins material.</p>  <p>In this lesson we focus on checks.</p>  <p><strong>What do you have to do?</strong><br />Give check and to force the king in an unfavorable spot. Subsequently&nbsp;win material with a skewer or a discovered attack.</p>","assignment":"","stickerID":74,"examples":[],"puzzles":[{"id":75087,"fen":"8/8/8/P2rN2k/5PRp/r7/7K/8 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[#] [%csl Rd5,Rh5][%cal Gg5d5]} {Q=1} 1. Rg5+! Kh6 {Q=2} 2. Ng4+ (2. Nf7+) *","format":27,"texts":["Розрахунок з форсуваннями.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75056,"fen":"8/8/kp1N4/8/6p1/3R2P1/B5K1/q3b3 w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Ra1,Ga2,Ga3][%evp 0,5,885,893,900,908,918,921]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1. Ra3+ ! Ba5 {Q=2} 2. Bc4+ Ka7 3. Rxa1 *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75091,"fen":"1r1r1k2/6p1/7p/2p5/2P5/q2B3P/5PP1/3QR2K w - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Ra3,Rf8][%cal Gf3a3][%evp 0,5,653,674,687,697,688,702]} {[#]} 1. Qf3+ ! Kg8 2. Bh7+ Kxh7 3. Qxa3 *","format":27,"texts":[],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75057,"fen":"7R/1kp4b/4r3/8/5N2/4nNPK/8/8 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Gh6,Gh7,Rh8][%evp 0,5,-604,-633,-633,-633,-643,-645]} {[#]} {Q=1} 1... Rh6+ ! 2. Nh4 {Q=2} Bf5+ 3. Kh2 Rxh8 *","format":27,"texts":["Розглянемо форсування.","Використовуйте відкритий напад."],"text":"","isMulti":0,"multiThemes":[]},{"id":75260,"fen":"r7/2p5/2k5/n7/4P3/8/1P6/K5Q1 b - - 0 1","pgn":"{[%csl Ra1,Rg1][%cal Ga1g1] [#]} {Q=1} 1... Nb3+ ! 2. Kb1 {Q=2} Ra1+ 3. Kc2 Rxg1 *","format":27,"texts